1
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:11,120
And take a step back and look at it.

2
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:24,280
Anyone short on cash, come to me.

3
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:28,940
Not that I've got any, but don't worry.

4
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:32,820
Look at the blue sky,

5
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:36,100
white clouds.

6
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:43,080
Love at first sight with a lemon

7
00:01:57,340 --> 00:01:59,860
Guess I'll try patrolling
the opposite way today.

8
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:00,980
Back alleys and such.

9
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:11,220
Isn't that Electrode Plus?

10
00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:16,600
Hey, Electrode Plus!

11
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:18,460
A police officer!

12
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:19,940
Riding around in a patrol car and all.

13
00:02:19,940 --> 00:02:22,360
Did you commit some crime or something?

14
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:24,180
Figures, coming from you.

15
00:02:24,180 --> 00:02:27,440
You must've done some hacking
or shady online business, right?

16
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:29,300
How rude.

17
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:32,580
Because today there's a PC class
being held at Katsushika station,

18
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:34,520
I was invited to teach it as the instructor.

19
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:41,760
Because you, the instructor Plusk, are a pro hyper
elementary schooler when it comes to computers, you know.

20
00:02:45,060 --> 00:02:52,260
Well, well, Professor Electrode, welcome! All of
us at the Katsushika station warmly welcome you!

21
00:02:53,120 --> 00:03:01,260
What's with that pathetic attitude? Even third graders know that!
Aren't you ashamed to be a police officer? Shut up!

22
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:05,380
Today, so that even us
old men can understand,

23
00:03:05,380 --> 00:03:08,420
we're going to have Professor Electrode
gently teach us about the internet.

24
00:03:08,420 --> 00:03:11,580
What's wrong with welcoming
him properly like this?

25
00:03:11,580 --> 00:03:15,380
That's right, Ryotsu.
These days, it's the age of "aite."

26
00:03:15,380 --> 00:03:16,160
"Aite."

27
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:19,780
You don't even know "aite"? You're hopeless.

28
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:21,300
That's why you're no good.

29
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:25,500
Could "aite" perhaps mean IT?

30
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:26,680
Aaaaaah, a!

31
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:35,520
IT revolution and all that. IT, no, that IT... so it's not
"aite," it's IT.

32
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:40,420
Well, you could put it that way. So do you know what
"IT" means?

33
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:50,120
Ohara-kun and the others... Chief, you didn't really plan
to learn the internet without even knowing that, did you?

34
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:53,980
Don't make fun of me. When it comes to IT...

35
00:03:53,980 --> 00:03:55,320
When it comes to IT?

36
00:03:58,520 --> 00:04:01,260
I can't wait to see you! Just kidding!

37
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:07,497
Information technology,

38
00:04:07,547 --> 00:04:10,260
in other words, the technology of
information through personal computers.

39
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:15,220
Well, well, well,
Ohara-kun was just doing that very thing.

40
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:18,280
Did that gag I aimed for a laugh fall flat?

41
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:21,300
Common sense, common sense.

42
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:22,780
Common sense, off-key.

43
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:25,280
My gags are really falling flat today.

44
00:04:25,280 --> 00:04:27,720
No, no, that's pretty funny, Ora-kun.

45
00:04:28,980 --> 00:04:36,720
On top of that, computers are hopeless, English terms are hopeless, and jokes are hopeless.
Teaching these old guys must be rough for you.

46
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:43,280
No, if they actually learn it, they'll become good
customers for my company's and my father's company's products.

47
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:46,360
As always, that's a comment no elementary
school student should be able to make.

48
00:04:46,360 --> 00:04:49,140
Anyway, Electrode Plus, please this way.

49
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:52,500
Ohara-kun, carry the teacher's randoseru.

50
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:53,040
Yes.

51
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:54,100
That's quite all right.

52
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:55,900
Teacher, please don't hold back.

53
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:56,840
No, that's not it.

54
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:05,820
Ohara-kun.

55
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:08,940
I already told you I didn't need it.

56
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:12,380
What, you developed
another new hyper randoseru?

57
00:05:12,380 --> 00:05:12,840
Yes,

58
00:05:12,890 --> 00:05:17,140
the security system now activates just
when anyone other than the owner touches it,

59
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:18,800
I've improved it to work that way.

60
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:22,600
It's loaded with a PC,
practically a workstation.

61
00:05:23,220 --> 00:05:24,820
It's packed with machinery.

62
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:28,000
There are no notebooks or pencils,
are there?

63
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:30,620
That's because we type
everything on keyboards.

64
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,800
We don't carry any paper or pencils at all.

65
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:35,840
What do you do when you
catch a cold and miss school?

66
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:37,140
Back in the day,

67
00:05:37,140 --> 00:05:39,180
Chikichi, let me copy your notes.

68
00:05:40,260 --> 00:05:41,880
We don't do that sort of thing.

69
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:44,680
For what we need,
we borrow data from friends.

70
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:46,300
Let me take the data.

71
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:47,000
Sure.

72
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:49,940
Times sure have changed.

73
00:05:49,940 --> 00:05:52,040
There's a solo version too.

74
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:52,940
Solo version?

75
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:57,780
The solo version has different finger
movements for each hand than the keyboard one,

76
00:05:57,780 --> 00:05:59,160
so it's good exercise for your fingers.

77
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:01,660
The more you use your fingers,
the better it is for your brain, you know.

78
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:03,640
You're fixating on the strangest things.

79
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:06,660
Electrode Sensei,
please proceed with the lesson.

80
00:06:09,940 --> 00:06:10,340
Yes.

81
00:06:10,820 --> 00:06:11,600
Oh no.

82
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:14,440
We've started 3 minutes and 30 seconds late.

83
00:06:14,440 --> 00:06:16,540
I have cram school after this,
so let's hurry.

84
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,220
Please follow my lead.

85
00:06:19,260 --> 00:06:22,180
I'm curious how he'll
teach these middle-aged men.

86
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:25,320
Nakagawa,
shall we take a little peek in as well?

87
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:26,280
Yes, sure.

88
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:32,288
Whew,

89
00:06:32,338 --> 00:06:37,580
getting those techno-crap old geezers to understand the Internet,
you're really something.

90
00:06:38,140 --> 00:06:43,720
Matterhorn's out of the question, but they could
probably climb as far as the sixth station of Mt. Fuji.

91
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:46,840
I explain it plenty of other places too.

92
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:48,600
That's only to be expected.

93
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:49,920
Not cute at all, are you.

94
00:06:50,260 --> 00:06:53,460
Anyway,
we're already five minutes behind schedule.

95
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:56,880
Could you speed up so we
make it to cram school?

96
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:59,100
This hyper little elementary schooler...

97
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:01,680
Nakagawa, step on it even more!

98
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:02,360
Yes.

99
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:04,780
Hold on, Nakagawa, fly!

100
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:09,360
You there.

101
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:10,160
I won't take up much of your time.

102
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:16,020
Lemon

103
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:17,860
Kankichi.

104
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:20,700
What are you doing in a place like this?

105
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:24,120
This dog hurt its leg and it's bleeding.

106
00:07:24,820 --> 00:07:26,160
What should I do?

107
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:31,160
Alright, let's take it to the hospital.

108
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:32,400
Kankichi!

109
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:34,220
Nakagawa!

110
00:07:34,220 --> 00:07:35,040
You called?

111
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:38,220
Nakagawa,
take it to the animal hospital nearby.

112
00:07:38,220 --> 00:07:38,920
Understood.

113
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:41,640
Wait a moment! My cram school...

114
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:44,680
What about my cram school?

115
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:46,240
This is an emergency!

116
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:49,040
Which is more important, the puppy's
injury or your cram school class?

117
00:07:49,300 --> 00:07:53,680
Sorry, I know you're in a hurry.

118
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:56,080
I really want to save this puppy.

119
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:58,122
Nakagawa,

120
00:07:58,172 --> 00:08:01,660
Turn left here!

121
00:08:01,660 --> 00:08:03,480
But the car navigation says right?

122
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:05,240
Just go! It's a shortcut.

123
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:18,420
What's this pounding in my chest?

124
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:26,120
Good thing the dog's injury wasn't serious.

125
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:27,060
Yeah.

126
00:08:28,020 --> 00:08:31,280
Good thing we could reach
the owner right away too.

127
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:34,180
Yeah, the collar had a
phone number written on it.

128
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:37,180
I called his cell and the damn guy
came flying here in five minutes.

129
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:39,680
Email?

130
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:45,000
You're emailing me?
He's right in front of you. Talk to him.

131
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:50,340
It's Electrode Plus.
He lives in Kanda. He's my relative.

132
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:58,880
How old is he?
Stop asking me by email every time.

133
00:08:58,880 --> 00:09:00,260
Ask him yourself.

134
00:09:00,260 --> 00:09:03,140
Greet him properly.

135
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:05,920
Honestly.

136
00:09:11,200 --> 00:09:13,440
A business card?
Are you a salaryman or something?

137
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:15,280
Ten?

138
00:09:16,260 --> 00:09:19,180
Not ten, it's plus. Electrode Plus.

139
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:23,000
Ask him for his email address.

140
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:26,520
I said stop sending me emails every time.
Ask him yourself.

141
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:34,080
Please.

142
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:36,129
Lemon-chan,

143
00:09:36,179 --> 00:09:39,520
Electrode Plus is asking
if you have a cell phone.

144
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:41,780
Don't use Nakagawa as a messenger!

145
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:43,220
I do, but why?

146
00:09:45,820 --> 00:09:47,160
He says he wants to borrow it for a bit.

147
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:49,700
Sure, I guess.

148
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:55,840
Alright, OK.

149
00:09:57,780 --> 00:09:58,500
Thanks.

150
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:01,340
Hello?

151
00:10:02,220 --> 00:10:04,040
I came up with an idea for new software,

152
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:06,160
so I attached it in an
email to your company address.

153
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:07,660
Got it. Checking it now.

154
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:10,820
I see. That's pretty interesting.

155
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:13,520
Let's consider it at
the next planning meeting.

156
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:15,580
He's like a grown-up, isn't he?

157
00:10:15,580 --> 00:10:18,320
This guy owns three companies of his own.

158
00:10:19,180 --> 00:10:21,440
Oh no, it's time for cram school to start!

159
00:10:27,500 --> 00:10:29,120
Well, I'm busy, so see you later.

160
00:10:32,660 --> 00:10:33,940
G-goodbye.

161
00:10:35,700 --> 00:10:37,180
What a busy guy.

162
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:40,780
I think he's probably the busiest
elementary schooler in Japan.

163
00:10:40,780 --> 00:10:42,200
He's a strange one, isn't he?

164
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:47,820
Lemon's pretty strange too, the kindergartner
who can tell a dish's flavor in one bite.

165
00:10:47,820 --> 00:10:48,905
Lemon-chan,

166
00:10:48,955 --> 00:10:52,200
you're in luck.
Shall I take you home to Kanda's place?

167
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,840
Do as you see fit.

168
00:10:55,220 --> 00:10:57,520
This guy's a huge period drama fan.

169
00:10:58,660 --> 00:10:59,020
I see.

170
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:05,200
Hello?

171
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:09,640
That's odd, it cut off again.

172
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:13,200
Lemon, the bath is free now.

173
00:11:13,680 --> 00:11:14,580
What's wrong?

174
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,300
I keep getting calls from
someone since earlier.

175
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:21,080
Whenever I pick up, they hang up.
Is it a prank call?

176
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:26,640
Not an email. Let me take a look.
Yep, just as I thought.

177
00:11:28,380 --> 00:11:29,040
Who is it?

178
00:11:30,880 --> 00:11:32,060
Electrode 10?

179
00:11:32,640 --> 00:11:33,520
It's Plus.

180
00:11:33,980 --> 00:11:35,680
Not 10, but Plus?

181
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:37,540
What's up with Plus?

182
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:41,700
That Plus guy keeps
sending me loads of emails.

183
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:44,860
So what's an email?

184
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:49,700
It's exchanging letters using
a mobile phone or computer.

185
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:54,800
If it's letters, why not just use letters?
Plus really is a strange one.

186
00:12:10,820 --> 00:12:12,120
That Electrode Plus guy

187
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:16,120
keeps sending Lemon emails every day,
and she's totally confused.

188
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:17,020
Every day?

189
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:19,260
And every two hours.

190
00:12:19,260 --> 00:12:24,000
He keeps asking things like her birthday,
blood type, and favorite flower.

191
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:28,540
Maybe Electrode Plus
has a crush on Lemon-chan.

192
00:12:28,540 --> 00:12:32,560
No way.
Plus is nine, and Lemon is only five!

193
00:12:32,560 --> 00:12:35,600
Well, I don't think age matters in love.

194
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:38,300
Lemon doesn't even know
how to send an email,

195
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:42,180
so could you tell that Plus kid
it's pointless to keep sending them?

196
00:12:43,140 --> 00:12:44,340
Sigh.

197
00:12:55,060 --> 00:12:57,580
Even as a living creature, it's cute.

198
00:12:58,120 --> 00:12:59,080
What are you doing?

199
00:12:59,080 --> 00:13:03,760
What is it? Barging into my room
like that without permission.

200
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:05,240
I did knock, you know.

201
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:06,760
Want me to do it again?

202
00:13:08,300 --> 00:13:08,500
Ready?

203
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:10,420
What do you want?

204
00:13:10,780 --> 00:13:11,700
I see.

205
00:13:11,700 --> 00:13:12,860
So that's it!

206
00:13:13,220 --> 00:13:17,540
Looks like you've finally developed
normal feelings like a young man should.

207
00:13:17,540 --> 00:13:20,580
Though what you're doing is hardly normal.

208
00:13:20,580 --> 00:13:21,680
What are you talking about?

209
00:13:21,940 --> 00:13:24,720
Whenever I think of Lemon,
I can't get anything done.

210
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:25,260
Gulp!

211
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:26,780
I can't even sleep at night.

212
00:13:26,780 --> 00:13:27,580
Jolt, jolt!

213
00:13:27,580 --> 00:13:30,360
Your heart pounds like crazy, doesn't it?

214
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:32,600
How do you know that?

215
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:34,400
Weren't you sick?

216
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:39,340
Don't worry, that's just what boys
go through when they fall in love.

217
00:13:39,340 --> 00:13:42,260
When I was a kid,
I was like that all the time.

218
00:13:43,080 --> 00:13:43,400
Love.

219
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:47,340
Well, you know,
my strike zone is pretty wide.

220
00:13:47,340 --> 00:13:49,960
From Mitchan at the greengrocer's
to Tomi-san at the clog shop.

221
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:51,060
My heart was pounding and racing!

222
00:13:51,060 --> 00:13:52,000
So this is what love feels like?

223
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:55,180
So, Officer, why did you come to my place?

224
00:13:57,420 --> 00:14:01,140
I understand you've fallen for Lemon,
but stop sending her so many emails.

225
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:04,160
Normally, she'd reply, you know.

226
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:06,120
But I'm not getting any replies at all.

227
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:07,080
Of course you're not.

228
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:09,700
She carries a phone for security, you know.

229
00:14:09,700 --> 00:14:11,220
I'm not doing emails.

230
00:14:11,220 --> 00:14:13,160
Is that so?

231
00:14:13,860 --> 00:14:16,960
I was worried she didn't like me, I thought.

232
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:17,720
Thank goodness.

233
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:21,540
He seems to have been asking her
birthday and hobbies by email, though.

234
00:14:21,540 --> 00:14:24,520
For that kind of thing,
write a letter or ask her in person.

235
00:14:24,520 --> 00:14:25,280
But that's...

236
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:28,960
That's right, Officer, you're her relative,
so ask Lemon-chan for me.

237
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:30,360
Don't make me say the same thing twice.

238
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:32,460
Why should I be the one asking?

239
00:14:32,460 --> 00:14:36,040
If you get the answers for me,
I'll give you one of my computers.

240
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:37,840
What, really?

241
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:42,300
Yes, one of these is nothing to me.

242
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:48,600
Fine. So what am I supposed to ask?

243
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:52,620
I'll print the questions out from my computer now,
so please wait.

244
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:56,920
Okay, it's done.

245
00:14:57,480 --> 00:15:00,220
Make sure she answers all fifty questions.

246
00:15:00,220 --> 00:15:01,020
Please.

247
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:04,040
Leave it to me.

248
00:15:06,260 --> 00:15:09,360
Favorite flower... tulips, and

249
00:15:10,040 --> 00:15:12,300
Okay, the last question.

250
00:15:12,300 --> 00:15:15,380
Favorite type of man is...

251
00:15:16,260 --> 00:15:18,140
Th-that's a no comment.

252
00:15:19,620 --> 00:15:21,600
"No comment," it says.

253
00:15:23,260 --> 00:15:25,540
Okay, thanks for your cooperation. Bye now.

254
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:28,380
You two, go have a good romance.

255
00:15:46,860 --> 00:15:49,340
Hey, Plus,
what are you doing standing over there?

256
00:15:49,340 --> 00:15:52,460
Lemon-chan turned me down.

257
00:15:52,460 --> 00:15:53,140
What?

258
00:15:53,140 --> 00:15:53,240
What?

259
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:56,940
No matter how many times I ask
Lemon-chan to go out with me,

260
00:15:57,420 --> 00:15:58,760
she won't say yes.

261
00:15:58,760 --> 00:16:00,120
Not bad!

262
00:16:00,220 --> 00:16:02,640
Did you actually meet Lemon-chan
in person and talk to her?

263
00:16:03,020 --> 00:16:03,980
No, that's not it.

264
00:16:04,460 --> 00:16:06,520
I had the officers ask
her for me the other day.

265
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:09,660
Entering her answers to the
fifty questions into the PC...

266
00:16:10,020 --> 00:16:12,940
I made a dating simulation
of me and Lemon-chan.

267
00:16:13,580 --> 00:16:16,520
A dating sim? Very Plus of you.

268
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:20,660
But no matter how many times I play it,
Lemon-chan keeps turning me down.

269
00:16:20,660 --> 00:16:24,840
Sounds interesting.
Let me see that simulation.

270
00:16:31,780 --> 00:16:33,440
This is pretty thorough.

271
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:35,380
First, the date is a movie.

272
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:39,100
A period drama Lemon likes

273
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:41,460
I did find out what Lemon-san likes,
after all.

274
00:16:41,900 --> 00:16:43,120
Next is a meal.

275
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:50,080
Lemon is picky about her food, you know.

276
00:16:50,660 --> 00:16:53,260
Don't worry,
the data of a top-class chef is included.

277
00:16:53,260 --> 00:16:55,440
You've covered all the important bases.

278
00:16:55,440 --> 00:16:59,380
Next, for Lemon-san, who loves animals,
we're off to Ueno Zoo.

279
00:16:59,380 --> 00:17:03,160
You really did your homework.
Nothing's been overlooked.

280
00:17:03,700 --> 00:17:06,840
It's evening already. So this is Odaiba?

281
00:17:06,840 --> 00:17:08,920
You're not bad at this, you know.

282
00:17:11,860 --> 00:17:14,780
Watching the sunset from
the Ferris wheel in Odaiba,

283
00:17:14,780 --> 00:17:18,900
then presenting her with a
bouquet of her favorite tulips,

284
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:24,560
and confessing,
asking her to go out with me. But...

285
00:17:27,420 --> 00:17:31,380
As you can see, I get rejected.

286
00:17:33,980 --> 00:17:40,400
What's that supposed to mean? A typo? What a lonely game...
Enough already!

287
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:49,240
Love isn't a game, you idiot. Don't be disappointed just because you got dumped in a simulation game.
But I'm telling you this with plenty of romantic experience.

288
00:17:50,660 --> 00:17:55,040
Just charge at her and get shattered!
But, Officer, you're single, aren't you?

289
00:17:55,680 --> 00:18:02,160
If you get shattered, don't you just stay broken?
Shut up, mind your own business!

290
00:18:02,940 --> 00:18:13,060
Anyway, go see Lemon in person, tell her how you feel, and ask her to go out with you.
Well, that's impossible. If I see her face, I won't be able to say a word.

291
00:18:13,060 --> 00:18:15,740
You're usually so cocky, but how pathetic.

292
00:18:15,740 --> 00:18:17,280
Then write a letter.

293
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:18,900
Handwritten, too.

294
00:18:18,900 --> 00:18:20,300
I don't even have anything to write with.

295
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:22,020
Everything I do is keyboard input.

296
00:18:22,540 --> 00:18:24,040
What kind of grade schooler are you?

297
00:18:25,980 --> 00:18:26,300
Yes.

298
00:18:31,620 --> 00:18:33,240
I'll lend you some of my writing paper.

299
00:18:33,240 --> 00:18:34,020
Write it.

300
00:18:34,560 --> 00:18:35,820
Do I have to write it with a brush?

301
00:18:35,820 --> 00:18:37,740
Lemon likes period dramas, so

302
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:40,820
she'll probably like a
letter written with a brush.

303
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:44,160
I haven't written anything
since kindergarten.

304
00:18:45,260 --> 00:18:47,860
I'll use the Warpple
brush font as a reference.

305
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:51,380
What are you doing?
Don't rely on that kind of thing every time.

306
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:55,080
It doesn't matter if your handwriting is bad.
What counts is writing it with your heart in it.

307
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:56,440
Got it.

308
00:18:59,440 --> 00:18:59,800
Right.

309
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:08,080
Then just fax it.

310
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:11,280
No, wait!
We have to hand it to Lemon directly!

311
00:19:11,760 --> 00:19:13,220
In person?

312
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:14,760
Obviously!

313
00:19:15,680 --> 00:19:17,000
Like putting it in her mailbox?

314
00:19:17,220 --> 00:19:17,560
No way!

315
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,480
Then tie it to an arrow and
shoot it into Lemon-san's room.

316
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:21,700
What if she gets hurt?!

317
00:19:23,540 --> 00:19:25,460
You've come this far, so steel yourself.

318
00:19:29,540 --> 00:19:32,940
Miss, Ichiro-san is here with a guest.

319
00:19:33,360 --> 00:19:34,720
Show them in.

320
00:19:36,180 --> 00:19:37,060
Excuse me.

321
00:19:39,820 --> 00:19:41,040
Please, make yourself at home.

322
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:44,580
Something came up.

323
00:19:44,580 --> 00:19:45,780
Don't go home.

324
00:19:45,780 --> 00:19:49,920
For once,
you're actually acting like a human being.

325
00:19:49,920 --> 00:19:51,380
Just sit down.

326
00:19:53,980 --> 00:19:55,460
What do you want, Kankichi?

327
00:19:55,460 --> 00:19:57,080
This guy's trying to get to Lemon...

328
00:19:57,080 --> 00:19:59,660
I told you not to talk to her by email.

329
00:19:59,660 --> 00:20:01,840
Come on, hand over the letter you wrote.

330
00:20:02,620 --> 00:20:03,380
Hurry up.

331
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:08,780
Don't just hand it over in silence.
Are you a wind-up doll?

332
00:20:09,800 --> 00:20:12,080
You're usually so sweet-talking, though.

333
00:20:12,080 --> 00:20:14,300
You're way too tongue-tied
in front of the girl you like.

334
00:20:22,160 --> 00:20:22,920
Kankichi

335
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:24,320
What is it?

336
00:20:24,920 --> 00:20:27,000
The PC froze again.

337
00:20:27,460 --> 00:20:29,560
Again? I can't afford a new one.

338
00:20:29,560 --> 00:20:32,460
If you like, I can fix it.

339
00:20:33,380 --> 00:20:33,680
Hey.

340
00:20:35,340 --> 00:20:37,360
The storage is full, so it's running slowly.

341
00:20:37,740 --> 00:20:40,100
I'm defragmenting it to
clean up the inside right now.

342
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:42,880
You don't need to get a new one?

343
00:20:42,980 --> 00:20:43,600
No, it's fine.

344
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:45,520
By deleting the unnecessary data

345
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:47,880
freeing up some space will be enough.

346
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:50,340
He says we don't have to buy a new one.

347
00:20:50,340 --> 00:20:51,840
I see.

348
00:20:54,680 --> 00:20:56,220
Looks like it's fixed.

349
00:20:57,900 --> 00:20:59,960
Since you can still add more memory,

350
00:20:59,960 --> 00:21:02,040
I'll put in some of my PC's memory.

351
00:21:03,380 --> 00:21:05,220
Let's add 20 gigs of
storage to the data disk too.

352
00:21:05,940 --> 00:21:08,940
Thanks. You really know your stuff,
even though you're in elementary school.

353
00:21:08,940 --> 00:21:13,120
She's not just any elementary schooler. She runs three software companies,
after all.

354
00:21:15,040 --> 00:21:17,540
But a girl like this would
be good as a boyfriend.

355
00:21:19,860 --> 00:21:23,480
I'm thinking of going to see kabuki next week.
Want to come along?

356
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:33,240
I've been asked out on a date.

357
00:21:33,240 --> 00:21:36,340
At least nod, or say yes or no,
so I know what you mean.

358
00:21:38,240 --> 00:21:39,740
Don't reply by email.

359
00:21:46,860 --> 00:21:47,580
Understood.

360
00:21:47,980 --> 00:21:50,680
But I have one condition for going.
Is that all right?

361
00:21:53,060 --> 00:21:53,780
Condition?

362
00:21:56,480 --> 00:21:57,160
Mm.

363
00:22:12,480 --> 00:22:13,160
Hmm

364
00:22:13,160 --> 00:22:13,380
Hmm

365
00:22:13,380 --> 00:22:13,680
Hmm

366
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:19,760
Sounds like a situation
where someone would be around

367
00:22:22,760 --> 00:22:23,280
Aaaah

368
00:22:25,380 --> 00:22:28,840
Why does she require bringing
along such a lazy cop?

369
00:22:30,020 --> 00:22:37,820
Aaaah. The noisy cop's asleep too,
so this is a good chance.

370
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:40,520
So, what kind of man does she like?

371
00:22:42,560 --> 00:22:44,620
Nah, forget it.

372
00:22:45,340 --> 00:22:49,240
I'm too embarrassed to ask.
Right, let's do it by email instead.

373
00:22:50,480 --> 00:22:52,280
No, writing a letter on this paper

374
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:55,640
And there's no brush or ink either.

375
00:23:00,060 --> 00:23:01,960
Plus, what's the matter?

376
00:23:04,580 --> 00:23:06,300
Lemon-chan...

377
00:23:06,300 --> 00:23:09,000
Please tell us what type of man you like.

378
00:23:19,560 --> 00:23:21,440
A guy like Kankichi.

379
00:23:25,280 --> 00:23:27,060
Is it over already?

380
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:32,860
Yo!

381
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:37,060
Oh my god!

382
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:58,500
System error.

383
00:23:59,420 --> 00:24:00,720
Please restart.

384
00:24:29,420 --> 00:24:33,660
the strange feeling I felt

385
00:24:35,340 --> 00:24:39,540
so on the arcade street tiles

386
00:24:39,540 --> 00:24:45,300
I tried walking only on the black ones

387
00:24:48,120 --> 00:24:53,640
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone forgets

388
00:24:54,520 --> 00:24:57,640
the politicians with
their self-important faces

389
00:24:57,640 --> 00:25:00,900
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow

390
00:25:00,900 --> 00:25:03,920
Try turning

391
00:25:04,520 --> 00:25:06,500
at that corner

392
00:25:07,500 --> 00:25:11,700
you can meet everyone, everyone

393
00:25:13,580 --> 00:25:16,300
over there, it's Kame-ari

394
00:25:17,360 --> 00:25:19,640
surely it's Kame-ari

395
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:24,840
Come on, everyone, to our town!

396
00:25:25,980 --> 00:25:26,380
Thank you.

397
00:25:30,680 --> 00:25:32,860
What's this, Chief? Who's this old geezer?

398
00:25:32,860 --> 00:25:35,100
The new officer who just arrived.

399
00:25:35,100 --> 00:25:37,240
Old as he is, an officer is an officer.

400
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:39,660
I'm the senior constable, so I outrank you.

401
00:25:39,660 --> 00:25:42,380
I'll teach you everything,
so just follow me.

402
00:25:42,380 --> 00:25:46,040
Next time:
"Super Low Officer's Wonderful Day."

403
00:25:46,040 --> 00:25:47,200
Nice to meet you.

404
00:25:51,680 --> 00:25:54,000
Surely it's Kameari.

405
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:59,220
Come on, everyone, to our town!

406
00:26:00,300 --> 00:26:00,780
Thank you.

